## How to Use This Document

This is the **primary entry point** for custom AI agent work in the APAC region. It carries a reader through three states — from thinking about an agent, to designing it, to building it — and hands off to the detailed technical guides at the right moment.

```
   ADVISORY                 TECHNICAL WORKBOOK              DEVELOPMENT
   (this document)          (Design + Build narratives)     (build engine + hardening)
   ─────────────            ──────────────────────────      ──────────────────────────
   Should we build?         How will it be architected?     Build it, harden it, ship it.
   Which repo/service?      What decisions must we make?     Joule Cookbook + PathToProd
   L0-1 → L0-10 gates       Design & Build narratives        checklist, deploy, register
```

The document does not replace the build guides — it **governs and routes into them**. The detailed engineering material lives in the linked guides ([§13](#13-linked-guides--where-the-detail-lives)); this document tells you *when to engage, what to decide, and which gates to clear*.

### Where am I? — the engagement journey

| Stage | You are here when… | Exit criteria (move to next) | Primary owner |
|---|---|---|---|
| **1. Advisory** | Evaluating a custom AI opportunity; unsure of approach, repo, or feasibility. | Repository & service model selected; L0-1 onboarding cleared; executive/architecture sponsorship confirmed. | Data & AI Architecture Group |
| **2. Technical Workbook** | Approach agreed; now making architecture decisions and shaping the build. | Design Narrative signed off; Build Narrative sequenced; L0 gates for design/grounding/security reviewed. | Solution Architect + Architecture Group |
