## 1. Overview

As adoption of Agentic AI accelerates, organisations require more than development frameworks alone. Successful AI solutions must be **secure, scalable, compliant, maintainable, and aligned with enterprise architecture standards**.

The **Data & AI Architecture Group** provides architecture guidance, governance frameworks, reference architectures, and implementation best practices to support the successful design, deployment, and operation of custom AI agents.

Our objective is to help teams move **from experimentation to enterprise-grade production deployments** through consistent architecture patterns, governance controls, and reusable accelerators.

> This document is the formal reference for how custom AI agents are architected, governed, and taken to production across the APAC region. It centres on the **Agent Governance Framework (L0-1 → L0-10)** — the mandatory review checklist that every custom agent initiative must satisfy before go-live — and routes builders into the **Technical Workbook** and **Development** guides that execute against those gates.

