## 6. The Governance Layer

While the available repositories provide implementation guidance, **governance remains a critical, separate responsibility**.

Both repositories focus on **how to build** agents. Neither repository provides an independently enforced governance layer covering architecture governance, security, compliance, responsible AI, production readiness, operational resilience, and lifecycle management.

**The Data & AI Architecture Group fills this gap** by providing governance frameworks, review processes, and architecture oversight throughout the agent lifecycle. The governance layer sits *above* the build engine (the Joule Cookbook) and the process wrapper (Agent Program) — see [§13](#13-linked-guides--where-the-detail-lives).

