## 9. Technical Workbook — Design Narrative

> **Purpose of this section:** As a team moves from *advisory* to *build*, this document becomes a **technical workbook**. The Design Narrative captures the architecture decisions that must be made *before* code is written. Each decision maps to a governance gate above and is detailed in the linked build guide ([§13](#13-linked-guides--where-the-detail-lives)).

The Design Narrative is the record of **how the agent will be architected**. It exists to make the design resilient: isolate the parts most likely to change (model provider, connectivity, region) so a later swap is configuration, not a rewrite.

### 9.1 Core design decisions

| Decision | Options | Guiding principle | Relates to gate |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Model access** | `aicore` (SAP AI Core / GenAI Hub) · `openai-compatible` (approved gateway) | Isolate the model behind a single `LLM_PROVIDER` switch — swapping provider or region is config-only, never code. | L0-2, L0-4 |
| **Connectivity mode** | Mock · Agent Gateway · Direct (Destination + Connectivity) | Build Agent Gateway (ORD/MCP) first — it is the standard tool-registration format. Direct is the fallback for on-prem / unregistered endpoints. | L0-6, L0-8 |
| **Grounding strategy** | Live transactional (OData) · Document RAG (HANA Vector) · Knowledge Graph (HANA RDF) | Choose per data shape: KG vs RAG is an explicit decision, not a default. | L0-3, L0-9 |
| **Identity model** | Technical user · Principal propagation | Interactive advisory agents usually need principal propagation so SAP authorisations apply per user — a broad technical user can leak data even read-only. | L0-5 |
| **Region / residency** | Commercial (GA) · Sovereign / regulated | Verify service availability (Joule, AI Core, AGW, HANA) in the target subaccount *before* designing around it; AI Core region must match SAP data residency. | L0-4, L0-5 |
| **Transport** | A2A (JSON-RPC over HTTP) | A2A is the standard agent surface — the single communication layer between Joule, external agents, and your agent. | L0-7, L0-10 |
| **State** | In-memory (MVP) · Durable (HANA Cloud) | Externalise conversation state keyed by `contextId` + user identity where it must survive restarts. | L0-10 |

### 9.2 Design principles (platform-change resilience)

- **Isolate the model** behind one switch so provider/region swaps touch configuration only.
- **Author tools with stable ORD IDs** in `asset.yaml` from the start, via the EDMX → MCP → ORD pipeline — this keeps tool registration consistent and portable.
- **Keep the data path region-agnostic** — reading business data is a plain HTTP/OData call, independent of model region.
- **Advisory-only by design** — no `POST`/`PATCH`/`DELETE` to SAP; disclaimer on financial outputs; never fabricate data.
- **Design sovereign regions as first-class**, not an afterthought.

> **Design Narrative sign-off** is the exit criterion for the Technical Workbook stage. The full architectural detail — connectivity modes, model isolation, identity propagation, regional handling — lives in the Joule Cookbook build guide (Part A). See [§13](#13-linked-guides--where-the-detail-lives).

