## 10. Technical Workbook — Build Narrative

The Build Narrative is the record of **how the agent will be executed** — the ordered path from empty folder to a Joule-registered, production-hardened agent. It is the bridge from *workbook* into *development*.

### 10.1 The build sequence

| Step | What happens | Detailed in |
|---|---|---|
| **1. Scaffold** | Generate the project skeleton (Joule Studio bootstrap or a generated accelerator boilerplate). | Cookbook Part A §2 |
| **2. Mock-first** | Make the full agent work offline in mock mode before any SAP connection — all tests pass with no credentials. | Cookbook Part A §3 |
| **3. Connect data** | Wire the chosen connectivity mode (Agent Gateway / Direct); run the EDMX → MCP → ORD pipeline. | Cookbook Part A §3, §5 |
| **4. Harden** | Auth & identity at the A2A boundary, error/resilience contract, observability, security. | Cookbook Part A §3a, §3b, §1b |
| **5. Deploy** | Push to Cloud Foundry (or Kyma); bind services via `VCAP_SERVICES`. | Cookbook Part B §6, §6a |
| **6. Register** | Register the agent card with Joule (admin UI or Joule Studio CLI). | Cookbook Part B §7 |

### 10.2 The build & hardening checklist (link-out)

Execution against the Build Narrative is governed by the **Agent-PathToProd checklist** — a master, staged checklist (Stage 0 pre-build → production readiness sign-off) where each item is tagged `[code]` (harness-validated) or `[deploy]` (developer-validated), and each gate must pass before the next stage starts.

> The Agent-PathToProd checklist is **not reproduced here** — it lives in and is maintained with the build guide. This governance document routes you to it; it does not duplicate it. See [§13](#13-linked-guides--where-the-detail-lives).
>
> **Note on automation:** the `[code]`-tagged items in Agent-PathToProd are already machine-checkable. They are the concrete seed of the *automated governance* this Group is moving toward ([§12](#12-future-direction)) — design-time validation and automated assessments build directly on them.

