## 14. Supporting Reference — Target Agent Architecture (SAP BDC)

Custom agents are designed to operate within the SAP Business Data Cloud (BDC) reference architecture, which layers enterprise data and grounds AI in business context:

| Layer | Role |
|---|---|
| **Lake Storage** | Integrates SAP and non-SAP data across multi-cloud, hybrid, and on-premise environments. |
| **Intelligent Compute** | Unifies transactional and analytical workloads (SQL, Spark, multi-model). |
| **Knowledge Core** | Embeds business context via shared semantics, knowledge graphs, canonical models, and governed data products. |
| **Agents & Intelligent Applications** | AI agents leverage business context to act autonomously, orchestrated by **SAP Joule**. |
| **Governance** | End-to-end lineage, policy enforcement, data quality, and controlled access embedded throughout. |
| **Open Data Ecosystem** | BDC Connect enables zero-copy sharing across Snowflake, Databricks, Google BigQuery, and Microsoft Fabric. |

This layered foundation ensures that custom agents are grounded in **governed, context-rich enterprise data** — a prerequisite for passing the L0-3 (RAG Quality) and L0-9 (Knowledge & Data Grounding) gates.

